{
  "title": "Scurvy",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/9034/scurvy",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 18 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Scurvy is disease caused by severe Vitamin C deficiency which presents with joint effusions, swelling over long bones, bleeding gums, loosening of teeth, hematuria, and susceptibility to hemorrhage.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made based on history, clinical and radiological picture, and resolution of symptoms following vitamin C administration. Lab tests are usually not helpful.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is prompt administration of Vitamin C.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "8% of men and 6% of women in the US have vitamin C deficiency",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "male: female ratio is 4:3",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Bimodal age bracket",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**infants 5-10months**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "uncommon in infants <7mths who are being breast fed as breast milk has vitamin C",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "men >60 years",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "wrists, knees, sternal ends of ribs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "areas of rapid growth in children",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "elderly, especially men who live alone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "chronic malnutrition",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "overcooking destroys vitamin C",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "alcoholic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "smokers",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "malabsorptive conditions (Whipple's disease, inflammatory bowel disease, cancer chemotherapy)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "humans are unable to synthesize L-ascorbic acid because the enzyme L-gluconolactone oxidase is nonfunctional",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Vitamin C deficiency leads to decrease in **chondroitin sulfate and collagen** synthesis and repair",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "impaired intracellular **hydroxylation** of collagen peptides",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "net effect is altered bone formatin with the greatest effect occuring in the **metaphysis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "defect in **spongiosa** of the metaphysis at the growth plate",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "because the demand for type I collagen is greatest during new bone formation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "infant diet consisting of evaporated or condensed milk",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "\"tea and toast\" diet in elderly",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "malaise and fatigue",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "bone pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "myalgia, because of reduced carnitine production",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "bleeding",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "gum bleeding and loosening of teeth",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "hematuria",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "hematemesis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "hemorrhage",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "iron deficiency",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "petechiae and ecchymosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "joint effusions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/scurvy%20knee.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**swelling over long bones** because of subperiosteal hemorrhage",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/scurvy%20wrist.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**scorbutic rosary** (costochondral separation)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "angular step-off deformity in children",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/scorbutic%20rosary.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "differentiated from rachitic rosary, which is rounded and nodular",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/rachitic%20rosary.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "wrist radiographs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "sternal ends of ribs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "the white line of Frankel",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/wimberger.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/trummerfeld.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "widened **zone of provisional calcification**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "between epiphysis and metaphysis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Trummerfeld zone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/trummerfeld.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "transvese radiolucent band in the **metaphysis** adjacent to the Frankel line",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "also known as the scurvy line",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Wimberger ring",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/wimberger.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/trummerfeld.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "ring of increased density surrounding **epiphysis**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Pelkin spur and fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/wimberger.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/trummerfeld.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "metaphyseal spurs and fractures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "corner sign of Park",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/corner%20sign.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "metaphyseal clefts",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "thin cortices (\"pencil-point\" cortex)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/scurvy%20xr1.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "decreased trabeculae with **ground-glass osteopenia**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/scurvy%20xr1.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "subperiosteal elevation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9034/images/trummerfeld.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**epiphyseal separation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "fractures and dislocations",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The diagnosis is usually made based on history, clinical and radiological picture, and resolution of symptoms following vitamin C administration. Lab tests are usually not helpful.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Labs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "fasting serum ascorbic acid level is low",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Histology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "replacement of primary trabeculae with granulation tissue",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "areas of hemorhage",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "widening **zone of provisional calcification** of the physis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "vitamin C replacement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "signs and symptoms of scurvy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "chronic malnutrition",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "techniques",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "oral vitamin C at 250mg qid x 1 week in adults",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Excellent prognosis if treated early",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
